# Path to the "holy shit it's working" moment — SlayZone Chromium

**Goal**: See a real SlayZone surface render in the Chromium fork, with live data flowing from the Bun sidecar. First concrete proof that the whole Phase 1–6 foundation works end-to-end.

**Target surface**: `StatusBar` (simplest region: ~200 LoC, read-only, no interactive state)

**Target timeline**: 1–3 days of agent work. 1 incremental build (~20–40 min). No full rebuild needed.

**Target endpoint**: launch the fork, open `chrome://slayzone-statusbar/`, see the real StatusBar React component rendering live data identical to the current Electron app.

---

## Prerequisites — all done (Phases 1–6 complete)

- Chromium 148.0.7778.40 fork builds + signs + launches on arm64 Mac
- 10 layout regions render as placeholders
- Shared packages shipping: design-tokens, ui-kit, mojo-bindings, state, rpc-client, dev-harness, test-harness
- Bun sidecar server: JSON-RPC over Unix socket, 468 handlers host-routed
- C++ SlayzoneSidecarClient shim: connects + retries on socket miss (Phase 2.3)
- Layout shell: region routing via `SlayzoneLayoutShell` (Phase 5.1) — swappable per-region
- Inline tab widget + TabStripModel wiring (Phase 6.2) — for future surfaces that need real tabs
- Patch series 0001–0016 applies cleanly; scheme handler factory + dedicated WebUI controllers work (Phase 6.3)

